From 4ca5a59d64c6ad825b83bfe0fcde849460be91ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Jun 2026 10:57:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00916/11171] [outer-loop] ARC verifier v2: cheap content
 ceiling LIFTED (7 invariant families, verified)

Ultracode workflow (8 agents) extended the C v1 ARC grid verifier with 7 relational
invariant families (object_count, palette_histogram, delta_pattern, content_overlap,
color_mapping, symmetry, tiling_scaling), measured each vs the same gold-vs-distractor
protocol, and combined them. A cheap, NON-INDUCING, gold-blind, cross-validated (OOF
logistic + applicability-flagged mean) combined verifier rejects ALL FOUR hard content
distractors >=0.73, where v1 was near-chance on 3:
  perturbed_gold 0.006->0.92, color_swap 0.38->0.85, transpose 0.29->0.73, wrong_dim 0.86->0.95.

Adversarially verified by the outer loop: family_score is gold-blind (execution-checked,
no solutions/gold access inside any scorer), the combined numbers reproduce on an
independent re-run, and the abstain-convention confound (naive min/max would read an
abstaining family as "perfectly consistent") is correctly handled via per-task
applicability flags.

Irreducible residual = SQUARE-grid transpose (ambiguous without the rule) + variable-dim
non-positional tasks -> genuine rule-INDUCTION (the generator's job). So the north-star
verifier-prunes/generator-induces boundary HOLDS, but the verifier's cheaply-prunable
share is now much larger -> efficiency-axis win for the ARC harness (reject most wrong
candidate OUTPUTS cheaply, not just malformed ones). Registry: arc_grid_combined_verifier
(v2, candidate). NEXT: wire into the interactive harness as candidate-output pruner; test
on ARC-2. No LLM, no GPU, no submission.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
